Third-party research acknowledgements
================================================================================

The Anthropic OAuth body-fingerprint mimicry implemented in
internal/proxy/oauth_inject_waf_full.go was guided by reverse-engineering
research originally documented and published by the open-source project
sub2api (https://github.com/Wei-Shaw/sub2api), released under the
GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3.0.

The sub2api project documented the publicly-observable wire-format facts
that real Claude Code CLI traffic carries on Anthropic's OAuth path,
specifically:

  - the cc_version trailing 3-hex fingerprint is derived from
    SHA-256(constant-salt || sampled-bytes-of-first-user-text || cli-version);
  - the cch field is an xxhash64 digest of the marshalled body keyed by
    a constant 64-bit seed;
  - the byte indices [4, 7, 20] are the canonical sample positions used
    by the upstream client.

These are observable protocol facts (not original creative expression of
sub2api) and are used here purely to interoperate with Anthropic's WAF
gating of premium models for non-Claude-CLI clients.

The Go implementation in this repository is an independent re-expression
written from the protocol specification: it uses different function
decomposition, different parsing idioms (two-stage RawMessage parse,
byte-level surgical placeholder rewrite without regex back-references,
streaming SHA-256 input), and different naming and helper structure than
sub2api's reference implementation. As a defensive measure, a copy of
the LGPL-3.0 license text is shipped under
THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES/sub2api-LGPL-3.0.txt.

If you redistribute aikey-proxy together with any code derived from
sub2api (rather than the independent re-expression here), the LGPL-3.0
obligations from that project apply to the derived portions; the
independent re-expression in oauth_inject_waf_full.go is contributed
under the same Apache-2.0 license that covers the rest of this module.
